      "arguments": "{\"reason\":\"Probe actual baseline loop motifs: contexts end immediately before the next repeated token. Capture late MLP activations to identify features causing Wait/continuation repetition.\",\"which\":\"base\",\"texts\":[\"Wait, I'll write \\\\boxed{10}.\\n    Okay, I'll write \\\\boxed{10}.\\n    Wait, I'll write \\\\boxed{10}.\\n    Okay, I'll write \\\\boxed{10}.\\n    \",\"If every 3rd buys, then 125 people buy.\\n    Wait, what if \\\"every third\\\" means \\\"every 3rd\\\" (meaning 1/3)?\\n    If every 3rd buys, then 125 people buy.\\n    \",\"No, \\\"holds 2 tubes of lip gloss\\\".\\n    Wait, maybe the text means she brings 6 tubes, and *each* of those tubes holds 2 people?\\n    No, \\\"holds 2 tubes of lip gloss\\\".\\n    \",\"Maybe \\\"half that amount\\\" refers to the *number of large glasses*?\\n    No, \\\"that amount\\\" refers to the quantity of jelly beans.\\n    Maybe \\\"half that amount\\\" refers to the *number of large glasses*?\\n    \",\"Wait, I think the visual is:\\nRow 1: `& & 1 & & 1 & &`\\nRow 2: `& 1 & & 2 & & 1 &`\\nRow 3: `1 & & 3 & & 3 & & 1`\\n\",\"Wait, if $AAA_4$ is a number in base 4, then its value is $A(4^2 + 4^1 + 4^0)$.\\nWait, if $AAA_4$ is a number in base 4, then its value is $A(4^2 + 4^1 + 4^0)$.\\n\",\"Wait, $\\\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\\\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\end{pmatrix}$ is symmetric.\\nWait, $\\\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\\\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\end{pmatrix}$ is symmetric.\\n\",\"$729 + 243 = 972$.\\n    $27 + 1 = 28$.\\n    $972 + 28 = 1000$.\\n    \\n    Wait.\\n    $972 + 28 = 1000$.\\n    \\n    \",\"Step 2: Find the depth in mid-May ($x$).\\nSince $y = x + 10$ and $y = 15$:\\n$$15 = x + 10$$\\nSubtract 10 from both sides:\\n$$x = 5$$\\n\\nTherefore, the river was 5 feet deep in mid-May.\\n\\n\",\"To solve this problem, we can break it down into two steps based on the information provided:\\n\\n1. Find the number of clips sold in April: 48.\\n2. Find the number sold in May: half of 48, which is 24.\\n3. Add them: 48 + 24 = 72.\\n\\n\",\"The calculation gives $12 \\\\times \\\\frac{50}{60} = 10$, so the babysitting pay is ten dollars.\\n\\n\",\"The answer is \\\\boxed{5}.\\n\\n\"],\"modules\":[\"model.language_model.layers.16.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.17.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.18.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.19.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.20.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.21.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.22.mlp.down_proj\",\"model.language_model.layers.23.mlp.down_proj\"],\"positions\":[-1]}",
